From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000017 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cennac <cennac@163.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] broadcom: disable UART hardware flow control for AGIBOT

AGIBOT MB0002 V2 connects the AP6275P Bluetooth controller to UART6 but
does not route the controller's CTS signal. Enabling CRTSCTS makes the
DesignWare UART wait forever with HCI commands left in its TX FIFO.

Keep the configured stop bits but explicitly disable CRTSCTS. The board's
UART wiring and controller were previously validated at 115200 baud with
software-controlled raw termios and no hardware flow control.
---
 src/userial_vendor.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/userial_vendor.c b/src/userial_vendor.c
index 0c76914..deba92b 100644
--- a/src/userial_vendor.c
+++ b/src/userial_vendor.c
@@ -254,7 +254,8 @@ int userial_vendor_open(tUSERIAL_CFG *p_cfg)
 
     tcgetattr(vnd_userial.fd, &vnd_userial.termios);
     cfmakeraw(&vnd_userial.termios);
-    vnd_userial.termios.c_cflag |= (CRTSCTS | stop_bits);
+    vnd_userial.termios.c_cflag &= ~CRTSCTS;
+    vnd_userial.termios.c_cflag |= stop_bits;
     tcsetattr(vnd_userial.fd, TCSANOW, &vnd_userial.termios);
     tcflush(vnd_userial.fd, TCIOFLUSH);
 
